<title>SOUTH KOREA: Ssangyong Sec union to strike for 1 hour.</title>
<headline>Ssangyong Sec union to strike for 1 hour.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ssangyong Investment and Securities Co's unionised workers will join nationwide strikes for one hour on Wednesday afternoon, a union official said.</p>
<p>&quot;This strike will be from 1 p.m. to 2 p.m. (0400-0500 GMT), and will affect all union members except for those handling direct customer trades,&quot; the official said, declining to be named. &quot;Customer trading will not be affected.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;We have not yet decided whether the strike will continue. We'll take it on a day-by-day basis,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>The Ssangyong Securities union has 1,400 members.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
